theory.intro:
The $x$-intercept is where a line crosses the $x$-axis, and the $y$-intercept is where it crosses the $y$-axis. Read them off a graph, or identify them from a table.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-1.5,0) -- (3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.3) -- (0,4.0) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->] (-0.3,3.36) -- (3.2,-0.84);
\fill (0,3) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (2.5,0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right,xshift=4pt] at (0,3) {$(0,\,b)$};
\node[below left,xshift=-4pt] at (2.5,0) {$(a,\,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
Identify the $x$- and $y$-intercepts of the line shown.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{lineblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[color=gridgrey,xstep=8mm,ystep=8mm] (-3,-1) grid (2,4);
\draw[<->,black] (-3.3,0)--(2.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-1.3)--(0,4.3) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2}{\draw[black] (\v,0.08)--(\v,-0.08);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\v,-0.08) {$\v$};}
\foreach \v in {-1,1,2,3,4}{\draw[black] (0.08,\v)--(-0.08,\v);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.08,\v) {$\v$};}
\node[below right,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,<->,color=lineblue] (-1.9,-0.8)--(0.4,3.8);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
The line crosses the $x$-axis halfway between $-2$ and $-1$, where $y=0$.

$x$-intercept: $(-1.5,0)$.

The line crosses the $y$-axis at $3$, where $x=0$.

$y$-intercept: $(0,3)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{lineblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[color=gridgrey,xstep=8mm,ystep=8mm] (-3,-1) grid (2,4);
\draw[<->,black] (-3.3,0)--(2.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-1.3)--(0,4.3) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2}{\draw[black] (\v,0.08)--(\v,-0.08);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\v,-0.08) {$\v$};}
\foreach \v in {-1,1,2,3,4}{\draw[black] (0.08,\v)--(-0.08,\v);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.08,\v) {$\v$};}
\node[below right,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,<->,color=lineblue] (-1.9,-0.8)--(0.4,3.8);
\fill[color=lineblue] (-1.5,0) circle (2pt);
\fill[color=lineblue] (0,3) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (-1.5,0) {$(-1.5,0)$};
\node[right,xshift=3pt] at (0,3) {$(0,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

